  "text": "I'll start by reading the package and the failing tests so the fixes follow the documented behaviour.The tests fail because negative amounts format with the wrong sign, dates swap the month and the day, and item ranking uses the wrong order. I will fix those three causes.`python3 run_tests.py` passes 6 of 6 tests.\n\n- `format_cents` used negative cents in the dollar math. -5 cents formatted as `-$-1.95`. The function now formats the absolute cents. It writes `-` before `$`. -5 cents now formats as `-$0.05`.\n- `parse_date` returned `(year, day, month)`. It now returns `(year, month, day)`.\n- `top_items` sorted the smallest total first. It now sorts the largest total first. When totals are equal, names sort from a to z.",
